-      "text": "Import documents and worksheets Open Setup & builders → Import a document , or use a card’s Import existing action. Documents become editable proposals before anything is saved. Supported files PDF (including clear scans), Word DOCX, Excel XLSX/XLSM, CSV/TSV, TXT, Markdown, and single-page PNG/JPEG/TIFF/WebP images. Use one file up to 12 MB. Save older DOC/XLS files as DOCX/XLSX first. Review the type and worksheet Choose the source and OCR language, or open Use copied document text and paste readable text. Reading the file does not save company records. Review the suggested destination: checklist, maintenance routine, toolbox-talk form, logbook design or inventory. For an inventory workbook, select the item worksheets to combine, review each mapping and location, and choose a new or existing inventory. Other types use one worksheet at a time. Names, source-row counts and suggested types are shown separately. Import another sheet separately if it has a different purpose. Hidden worksheets are named in the extraction notes and skipped. For inventory, choose the header row and map columns. Apply the mapping, then review or edit the tab-separated rows. Unmapped columns remain in the source preview. Blank quantities stay unknown. Box parents must match an explicitly marked box’s asset reference in the selected sheet. Edit the proposal. Checklists and routines show editable sections, checks, instructions, warnings, required tools, stages and answer fields. Open a check’s details to review its source reference, guidance and answer format. Move a proposed check into instructions or warnings when it does not need an answer, or move an instruction into the checks when it does. Toolbox forms need discussion prompts, understanding questions and an acknowledgement declaration. Logbooks use one field per line: Label | type | unit | required | choices separated by semicolons. Supported field types are text, number, date, time and select. Open the complete extracted text and extraction notes. Check spelling, numbers, units, row order and anything omitted against your original document. Choose Check edited draft , review the summary and confirm your review. Save the new definition or separate list, then open the exact saved result. Instructions, tools and answers Review description and purpose separately from operational checks. Required tools stay in the requirements. Before/after answer columns become two workflow stages; each check can apply to one or both. A checkbox confirms the check; Yes/No and other choices are separate answers, with blank meaning unanswered. Text and numeric readings retain their labels and units. Numeric limits stay unspecified unless the source supplies them or you deliberately add them. Filled answers, ticks and signatures in the source never become completed work. Word paragraph/table order and supported PDF form-field positions help identify structure. Plain text and scans use source wording and headings, so ambiguous or unusual layouts still need correction. Read all extraction notes and compare the complete source; automatic recognition does not approve a procedure. What is created Checklists, maintenance routines and toolbox forms are saved as unpublished drafts. Logbooks contain the reviewed fields with no imported entries. Inventory creates one new list from the selected item worksheets, or adds the reviewed new rows to a permitted existing inventory. Existing items and their verification, tasks and custody stay in place. This import does not record stock verification, department assignments, movement or Fleet custody. Keep the source file. This flow records its filename and SHA-256, but does not upload its original bytes to Original files . Upload the reference separately there if needed and permitted. Scans and difficult layouts The hosted container includes local OCR for English and Portuguese. OCR on other installations needs Tesseract; scanned PDFs also need Poppler. OCR supports clear printed text and needs review. Handwriting, poor photos, merged tables, unusual layouts and picture-only Office content may need manual correction. PDFs support up to 80 pages, including up to 12 scanned pages; spreadsheets support up to 25 worksheets and 50,000 stored cells. Split larger documents. Formulas, macros, links, queries and embedded objects never run. Permissions and interrupted saves Each destination follows your current builder permissions. Editing a checked draft invalidates its review. An open proposal is protected from navigation; save or close it first. If the save response is lost, use Retry unchanged request . The unchanged operation is checked for a previous saved result instead of creating another copy. Existing Wavelink packages Existing .ajcheck, .ajtoolbox, .ajlogs and .ajinventory packages still use their reviewed package-import path. Whole-company and completed-history transfers remain separate advanced tools. Importing a definition never completes a check, approves a procedure or signs a toolbox talk. Review how the source was interpreted In Setup & builders → Import a document , open Review source interpretation to compare uncertain passages with their available source locations. A Review control focuses the existing editor; it does not change wording or approve the draft. Original Excel rows and PDF page/printed-row labels are distinct from extracted table positions, blocks and text lines. Correct instructions, warnings, tools, answer types and before/after stages in the proposal. Printed Yes/No, Sim/Não and Pass/Fail labels may become choices; source ticks, historical answers and signatures never become completed work. An unspecified Status column still needs review. The panel records the original extraction and does not mark its points resolved merely because wording changed. A toolbox definition uses discussion prompts rather than separate checklist instruction/tool fields. Use Add instructions and tools to discussion to include their source wording in editable groups, then check the changed draft again. Native prompt limits apply; guidance is not silently shortened. Review the understanding questions, supervisor instruction and acknowledgement declaration before saving an unpublished form. Switching a worksheet shows that worksheet’s review points. Compare the complete source for missing material, and retain your original file. No import proves that every passage or layout has been recognized. Review boxes and their contents before import After mapping an inventory worksheet, open Boxes and contents . Review each included row's asset/tag reference, explicit box flag, parent box reference and expected quantity. Searching, paging and opening this view do not change the checked proposal. Editing a field requires checking the changed draft again. A parent must be an included, explicitly marked box with a unique asset/tag reference in the same worksheet . Use its exact reference, including leading zeros and punctuation, or choose No container deliberately. A name, serial number, part number, indentation or the word BOX does not establish a relationship. References across worksheets or to boxes already in the destination inventory are not resolved during this import. Review missing or excluded parents, duplicate references, self-links, cycles and excessive depth. A box describes one container; use an expected quantity of one or leave it Unknown when appropriate. Ordinary stock can have zero or another valid expected quantity. No imported quantity is a completed stock verification. Contained rows inherit their top box's effective location. The checked import summary uses that location before saving, and a differing mapped location is retained in Notes. Review this together with worksheet locations. A location note records the reviewed mapping; it is not proof of a physical move. Explicit parent and box-flag headers help suggest inventory. Unqualified Box/Container ID or reference headers can identify the row itself or its parent, so map them deliberately as an asset/tag or parent reference. Unmapped source columns remain available as source notes. Field edits keep full mapped row order, original row references when available and item choices. Reapplying a mapping replaces the mapped values and these corrections; editing the complete table can reset source references and choices. Review the visible notice before continuing. Pending or uncertain saves must retain their unchanged retry request. Review table instructions and sections Clearly labelled descriptions, instructions and required tools can be retained from label-and-value tables or labelled rows inside a check table. Before and after headings and changed printed column headers help organize the following checks. Read Review source interpretation and compare the proposed wording, stages and answer fields with the source before saving. A printed response definition can describe a new answer field; a completed response, signature or name is not a new answer. Unclear tables still require manual correction. For a toolbox talk, deliberately copy retained instructions and tools into discussion prompts when appropriate. Review source rows and header choices In Choose items , use Needs source review to inspect rows that resemble repeated headers, headings, summaries, instructions or footers. The advice describes the original extracted source. Rows remain included until you deliberately exclude them. Items can legitimately be called Total or Instructions; compare their identifiers and expected quantities with the source. The header selector includes the first 250 extracted nonempty rows. Open Find header row to search and page through any extracted row, compare its preview, and choose the actual column header. Original Excel row labels appear only when the extractor proves them. Review any notice about rows before the selected header or other header candidates. Changing the header requires applying the mapping and checking the changed proposal again. Editing the complete raw table clears source-row advice and provenance when they can no longer be established. Field corrections keep their original-source references, but do not turn the original advice into a statement about the corrected item. Source Counted columns remain Notes; the app performs stock verification. Review printed log column headings Log proposals use supported printed column headings rather than completed metadata rows. Review the date, time, event and physical reading fields against the actual source. Common unambiguous physical headings can propose numeric fields with their printed units; a previous measurement, vessel name or signature does not become a new field label or observation. If later printed headers change the table layout, compare the located advice in Review source interpretation with the source and edit the log fields. The proposal retains the first supported schema for that source table; separate or correct other layouts deliberately. Exact repeated headers do not add duplicate fields. Selected worksheets retain their own names. Unclear headings still need manual correction. Review Toolbox discussion tables Explicit Topic and Discussion points table columns can supply reusable discussion prompts. Compare the retained wording and located source review with the document. Completed answer, signature and attendee columns are excluded from new prompts and responses. The existing Toolbox form still requires deliberately reviewed understanding questions and a declaration. Importing a definition does not sign, complete or approve a meeting. Labelled instructions, tools and supervisor guidance remain available; use the existing instruction/tool copy action when those blocks should become discussion prompts. Correct one imported item without resetting choices In Choose items , open Edit item to correct that row's Name , Serial number (SN) or Part number (PN) . Apply a real change, then Check the proposal again. Cancel or an unchanged Apply retains the existing approval. Individual corrections keep deliberate exclusions, original source coordinates, full unchanged Notes and reviewed box relationships. Source-row advice still describes the original extracted wording; compare it with the corrected proposal and actual source. A field correction is not a quantity verification or proof that a row belongs in stock. Source Counted columns remain Notes. Reapplying mapping replaces mapped corrections; editing the complete mapped TSV can reset selection and clear provenance, as its notice explains. Keep corrections while reviewing worksheets. Switching Inspect worksheet only changes the worksheet you are inspecting. A completed check, its import overview and your confirmation stay available. Changing included sheets, locations, destination or item fields still requires Check edited draft again. Before Apply mapping replaces manually corrected names, SN/PN, quantities or box relationships, review the warning for that worksheet. Cancel keeps the corrected rows. Confirm replaces corrections for that worksheet with mapped source values and requires another check. During an uncertain save, retry the unchanged request before changing the proposal. Navigate the inventory review. Inspect worksheet and each worksheet’s Inspect mapping and items button change only the sheet on screen. Worksheets to import shows the checkboxes that decide what will be saved; an excluded worksheet remains available for inspection. The review shortcuts open Worksheets, Mapping, Items, Boxes, Source or an available Import overview without changing the proposal. Source-column choices show column numbers so repeated headings can be distinguished. A pending-mapping notice explains that current item rows still use the last applied mapping. Review shared-column advice when two destination fields use the same source column; deliberate reuse remains available. Choose an item-name column before applying a mapping. Undo pending mapping choices without replacing corrected rows. Restore last applied mapping restores the recorded header and column choices for the worksheet you are inspecting. Current item edits, full Notes, row exclusions, source references and box relationships stay in place. The pending changes show which destination fields or header were changed. Restoration does not apply source values to the rows and requires Check edited draft again before saving. Apply mapping to rows still replaces mapped values and asks before replacing deliberate corrections. The restore action is unavailable if this draft has no recorded last-applied mapping; older drafts are not guessed from their item rows. Busy or uncertain saves remain locked; resolve an uncertain result with the unchanged retry.",
