-<details class="help-scope"><summary>About these instructions</summary><p>This reader standardises presentation, not the entire procedure library. The original instructions, version labels and warnings are retained. Some topics describe the local Windows hub or earlier interface labels. They must not be read as proof that all desktop setup, imports or recovery work is available in the hosted browser.</p><p>The full wording, hosted/local scope, native Help and PDF review remains on the development list. Use only company-approved operational procedures; viewing Help does not approve a checklist, release equipment or verify work.</p></details><details class="help-outline"><summary>On this page <span>5 sections</span></summary><ol><li class="level-h2"><a href="#browser-entry">Create or import directly from Inventory</a></li><li class="level-h3"><a href="#help-section-1">Permissions</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-review-boxes-and-their-contents-before-import">Review boxes and their contents before import</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-review-source-rows-and-header-choices">Review source rows and header choices</a></li><li class="level-h2"><a href="#help-correct-one-imported-item-without-resetting-choices">Correct one imported item without resetting choices</a></li></ol></details><article aria-label="Build an inventory" class="help-article"><section class="chapter" data-topic="inventorybuilder" id="inventorybuilder"><p class="kicker">User instructions</p><h1>Build an inventory</h1><p><strong>Import document items into one inventory.</strong> Choose a workbook from Setup &amp; builders, select the item worksheets, then review each mapping and its location. All selected sheets save into one new inventory. To add items to a saved inventory, choose Add to existing inventory or use its Import items action. Check again after changing included sheets, mapped rows, locations or the destination. Browsing another worksheet keeps the completed check. Builder, inventory-view and item-edit permissions are needed to add items.</p><h2 id="browser-entry">Create or import directly from Inventory</h2><p>In the hosted browser, <strong>Inventory &amp; boxes → Create inventory / Import existing</strong> opens the same permitted Setup &amp; builders flow. Create defines an empty list and locations; Import checks a supported .ajinventory package and shows the exact copy preview before saving. A permissioned non-administrator can use these actions. The native wizard instructions below describe the existing Windows workflow; they are not additional required browser steps.</p><p class="subtitle">Create the structure before entering stock</p><p>In the browser, use <strong>Setup &amp; builders → Inventory structure</strong> with the <strong>Build and import inventory structures</strong> permission. Administrators have this capability automatically, but administrator status is not required. The native Admin Inventory Builder remains available for its existing advanced workflow.</p><ol><li>Choose <strong>Create new</strong> in Setup &amp; builders, or open <strong>Inventory → List setup → Inventory Builder</strong> in native Admin. Enter the list name and purpose.</li><li>Add storage locations, one per line. Unassigned and In use are supplied automatically. Department custody uses existing project departments; manage those under Departments.</li><li>Add optional fields only when needed. Available types are text, number, date and dropdown choice. Item name, model, serial, part number, asset, quantity, dates, department and location are already included.</li><li>Review and select <strong>Create inventory</strong>. This saves an empty list, not an imported stock count. Add items or import a prepared inventory package separately.</li></ol><p>Back and Next retain changes inside the open wizard. Nothing is saved until Create inventory. Cancel asks before discarding unsaved builder changes. Additional-field structure is fixed after creation; locations can be added later through Locations.</p><h3 id="help-section-1">Permissions</h3><p>Browser creation/import needs <strong>Builders &amp; imports → Build and import inventory structures</strong> together with its inventory dependency. An administrator can grant that capability to a Technician or Supervisor without making the person an administrator. View inventory, Add and edit items, Move items, Run stock verifications and Export reports remain separate permissions.</p><p>By default, technicians can view inventory and check stock; supervisors can also add/edit and move items. Administrators have full access. Department membership is not a substitute for an application permission.</p></section><section id="ui107-boxes-and-contents"><h2 id="help-review-boxes-and-their-contents-before-import">Review boxes and their contents before import</h2><p>After mapping an inventory worksheet, open <strong>Boxes and contents</strong>. Review each included row's asset/tag reference, explicit box flag, parent box reference and expected quantity. Searching, paging and opening this view do not change the checked proposal. Editing a field requires checking the changed draft again.</p><p>A parent must be an included, explicitly marked box with a unique asset/tag reference in the <strong>same worksheet</strong>. Use its exact reference, including leading zeros and punctuation, or choose <strong>No container</strong> deliberately. A name, serial number, part number, indentation or the word BOX does not establish a relationship. References across worksheets or to boxes already in the destination inventory are not resolved during this import.</p><p>Review missing or excluded parents, duplicate references, self-links, cycles and excessive depth. A box describes one container; use an expected quantity of one or leave it Unknown when appropriate. Ordinary stock can have zero or another valid expected quantity. No imported quantity is a completed stock verification.</p><p>Contained rows inherit their top box's effective location. The checked import summary uses that location before saving, and a differing mapped location is retained in Notes. Review this together with worksheet locations. A location note records the reviewed mapping; it is not proof of a physical move.</p><p>Explicit parent and box-flag headers help suggest inventory. Unqualified Box/Container ID or reference headers can identify the row itself or its parent, so map them deliberately as an asset/tag or parent reference. Unmapped source columns remain available as source notes.</p><p>Field edits keep full mapped row order, original row references when available and item choices. Reapplying a mapping replaces the mapped values and these corrections; editing the complete table can reset source references and choices. Review the visible notice before continuing. Pending or uncertain saves must retain their unchanged retry request.</p></section><section id="ui108-inventory-source-review"><h2 id="help-review-source-rows-and-header-choices">Review source rows and header choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, use <strong>Needs source review</strong> to inspect rows that resemble repeated headers, headings, summaries, instructions or footers. The advice describes the original extracted source. Rows remain included until you deliberately exclude them. Items can legitimately be called Total or Instructions; compare their identifiers and expected quantities with the source.</p><p>The header selector includes the first 250 extracted nonempty rows. Open <strong>Find header row</strong> to search and page through any extracted row, compare its preview, and choose the actual column header. Original Excel row labels appear only when the extractor proves them. Review any notice about rows before the selected header or other header candidates. Changing the header requires applying the mapping and checking the changed proposal again.</p><p>Editing the complete raw table clears source-row advice and provenance when they can no longer be established. Field corrections keep their original-source references, but do not turn the original advice into a statement about the corrected item. Source Counted columns remain Notes; the app performs stock verification.</p></section><section id="ui109-inventory-item-corrections"><h2 id="help-correct-one-imported-item-without-resetting-choices">Correct one imported item without resetting choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, open <strong>Edit item</strong> to correct that row's <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Serial number (SN)</strong> or <strong>Part number (PN)</strong>. Apply a real change, then <strong>Check</strong> the proposal again. Cancel or an unchanged Apply retains the existing approval. Individual corrections keep deliberate exclusions, original source coordinates, full unchanged Notes and reviewed box relationships.</p><p>Source-row advice still describes the original extracted wording; compare it with the corrected proposal and actual source. A field correction is not a quantity verification or proof that a row belongs in stock. Source Counted columns remain Notes. Reapplying mapping replaces mapped corrections; editing the complete mapped TSV can reset selection and clear provenance, as its notice explains.</p></section><p id="ui111-inventory-review-safeguards"><strong>Keep corrections while reviewing worksheets.</strong> Switching <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> only changes the worksheet you are inspecting. A completed check, its import overview and your confirmation stay available. Changing included sheets, locations, destination or item fields still requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again. Before <strong>Apply mapping</strong> replaces manually corrected names, SN/PN, quantities or box relationships, review the warning for that worksheet. Cancel keeps the corrected rows. Confirm replaces corrections for that worksheet with mapped source values and requires another check. During an uncertain save, retry the unchanged request before changing the proposal.</p><p id="ui112-inventory-review-navigation"><strong>Navigate the inventory review.</strong> <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> and each worksheet’s <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> button change only the sheet on screen. <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows the checkboxes that decide what will be saved; an excluded worksheet remains available for inspection. The review shortcuts open Worksheets, Mapping, Items, Boxes, Source or an available Import overview without changing the proposal. Source-column choices show column numbers so repeated headings can be distinguished. A pending-mapping notice explains that current item rows still use the last applied mapping. Review shared-column advice when two destination fields use the same source column; deliberate reuse remains available. Choose an item-name column before applying a mapping.</p><p id="ui113-inventory-mapping-recovery"><strong>Undo pending mapping choices without replacing corrected rows.</strong> <strong>Restore last applied mapping</strong> restores the recorded header and column choices for the worksheet you are inspecting. Current item edits, full Notes, row exclusions, source references and box relationships stay in place. The pending changes show which destination fields or header were changed. Restoration does not apply source values to the rows and requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving. <strong>Apply mapping to rows</strong> still replaces mapped values and asks before replacing deliberate corrections. The restore action is unavailable if this draft has no recorded last-applied mapping; older drafts are not guessed from their item rows. Busy or uncertain saves remain locked; resolve an uncertain result with the unchanged retry.</p></article>
